## Quick Reference — What Each Tests

| Prompt Category | Tests |
|---|---|
| Simply Supported + UDL | Basic load diagram (flat line), symmetric SFD |
| Simply Supported + Point | SFD with step, BMD with peak at load point |
| Cantilever + UDL | Fixed support rendering, negative moment |
| Cantilever + Point | Max moment at fixed end |
| Overhang + UDL | Dual-support diagram, negative moment at support B |
| Overhang + Point at free end | Hogging over support B |
| Continuous (equal spans) | Symmetric support moments, uniform load diagram |
| Continuous (unequal spans) | Asymmetric moments, load diagram same value but different span widths |
| Continuous (fixed ends) | Zero moment at fixed ends, different SFD shape |
| Extreme loads | Beam auto-resize, deflection fixes |

> **Note**: The load diagram for continuous beams will appear as a flat horizontal line when all spans have the same UDL — this is correct. The SFD and BMD will vary across spans showing the structural behaviour.
